OVERVIEW: Organize DICOM files by study and series hierarchy

USAGE: dicom-study organize <input> --output <output> [--pattern <pattern>] [--copy] [--verbose]

ARGUMENTS:
  <input>                 Input directory containing DICOM files

OPTIONS:
  -o, --output <output>   Output directory for organized files
  --pattern <pattern>     Folder naming: 'descriptive' = <Patient's
                          Name>_<Study Description>_<last 8 characters of Study
                          Instance UID>/<Series Number>_<Modality>_<Series
                          Description>/<n>.dcm; 'uid' = <Study Instance
                          UID>/<Series Instance UID>/<n>.dcm (default:
                          descriptive) (default: descriptive)
  --copy                  Copy files instead of moving them
  -v, --verbose           Show verbose output
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

